  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">510. Rwanda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of 510.Rwanda, and its partners, is to transform people, organizations, nations, and devices into members of reliable digital ecosystems. Whilst the full potential of emerging technologies is far reaching in Rwanda and beyond, initial use cases will focus on local entrepreneurs and relevant public services, thereby reducing administrative costs of doing business and driving access to financing and inclusive economic growth. In the long run, the same system, and its ability to handle complex sets of data, can be expanded to other areas such as social security or local governments.As Rwanda has a limited physical infrastructure, digital infrastructure is helping to solve a number of problems. For example, digital infrastructure allows people to collaborate and receive services without lengthy commutes. For local operations, the company intends to hire local employees and create a technology-savvy ecosystem. These technology skills are easily transferable and increase the overall employability of the participants. With the support of DGGF financing, 510 aims kickstart this project, launch products and services in Rwanda, and hire the first employees. 510 aims to build out the organization with local talent, and will collaborate with local knowledge and educational institutes, ensuring growth of not only their employees, but also their partners.</narrative>
  </description>
